### 2. Test First (MUST BE FIRST)
Reference `400-testing-first.mdc` for detailed testing rules.

Write a `@WebMvcTest` using the skeleton's mock response shape as the expected output:
```java
@WebMvcTest(PostController.class)
class PostControllerTest {

    @Autowired MockMvc mockMvc;
    @MockBean PostService postService;

    @Test
    void createPost_returnsCreatedPost() throws Exception {
        UUID authorId = UUID.randomUUID();
        Post saved = new Post();
        saved.setId(UUID.randomUUID());
        saved.setTitle("Test Resource");
        saved.setContent("Test description");
        saved.setAuthorId(authorId);
        saved.setCreatedAt(Instant.now());
        given(postService.createPost(any(), eq(authorId))).willReturn(saved);

        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/posts")
                .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
                .content("""
                    {"title":"Test Resource","content":"Test description","authorId":"%s"}
                    """.formatted(authorId)))
            .andExpect(status().isOk())
            .andExpect(jsonPath("$.title").value("Test Resource"))
            .andExpect(jsonPath("$.postId").exists());
    }
}
```

Run the test — it MUST fail (controller still mocked / bean not wired).

### 3. Flyway Migration
Reference `vibe_database.md` for migration patterns.

Create migration following naming convention:
```
src/main/resources/db/migration/
└── V2__create_posts_table.sql
```

Migration must include:
- Table creation with proper columns
- Primary key (UUID, generated by the application layer via `GenerationType.UUID`)
- Foreign keys (if applicable)
- Timestamps (`created_at`, `updated_at`)
- Indexes for common queries
- `NOT NULL` constraints where appropriate

```sql
CREATE TABLE posts (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY,
    title VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,
    content TEXT NOT NULL,
    author_id UUID NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_posts_author_id ON posts (author_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_posts_created_at ON posts (created_at);
```

Flyway applies this automatically on application startup (`spring-boot-starter-jdbc` + `flyway-core` on the classpath). Verify manually:
```bash
./mvnw spring-boot:run
# check flyway_schema_history table for the new version
```

### 4. Domain Model (`@Entity`)
Reference `vibe_database.md` for JPA mapping conventions.

Create in `model/Post.java`:
```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "posts")
@Getter
@Setter
@NoArgsConstructor
public class Post {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.UUID)
    private UUID id;

    @Column(nullable = false, length = 200)
    private String title;

    @Column(nullable = false, columnDefinition = "TEXT")
    private String content;

    @Column(name = "author_id", nullable = false)
    private UUID authorId;

    @CreationTimestamp
    @Column(name = "created_at", updatable = false)
    private Instant createdAt;

    @UpdateTimestamp
    @Column(name = "updated_at")
    private Instant updatedAt;
}
```

### 5. Repository Implementation
Reference `vibe_database.md` for Spring Data query-method conventions.

Create in `repository/PostRepository.java`:
```java
public interface PostRepository extends JpaRepository<Post, UUID> {

    List<Post> findByAuthorIdOrderByCreatedAtDesc(UUID authorId);

    @Query("SELECT p FROM Post p WHERE p.title ILIKE %:keyword%")
    List<Post> searchByTitle(@Param("keyword") String keyword);
}
```

Implement only the methods needed for the current endpoint — `JpaRepository<Post, UUID>` already provides `save()`, `findById()`, `findAll()`, and `deleteById()` for free.

### 6. Service Layer
Create in `service/PostService.java`:

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class PostService {

    private final PostRepository postRepository;

    @Transactional
    public Post createPost(CreatePostRequest request, UUID authorId) {
        Post post = new Post();
        post.setTitle(request.title());
        post.setContent(request.content());
        post.setAuthorId(authorId);

        Post saved = postRepository.save(post);
        log.info("Created post {} for author {}", saved.getId(), authorId);
        return saved;
    }
}
```

### 7. Controller Replacement
Reference `500-implementation.mdc` for replacement patterns.

Replace the mock implementation in the API endpoint:
```java
// Before (Phase 0 mock)
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity<PostResponse> createPost(@Valid @RequestBody CreatePostRequest request) {
    PostResponse mock = new PostResponse(UUID.randomUUID(), request.title(), request.content(), request.authorId(), Instant.now());
    return ResponseEntity.ok(mock);
}

// After (Phase 1 real)
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity<PostResponse> createPost(
        @Valid @RequestBody CreatePostRequest request,
        @AuthenticationPrincipal UserDetails currentUser) {
    UUID authorId = UUID.fromString(currentUser.getUsername());
    Post created = postService.createPost(request, authorId);
    return ResponseEntity.ok(PostResponse.from(created));
}
```

### 8. Test Validation
Run the test — it MUST pass now:
```bash
./mvnw test -Dtest=PostControllerTest#createPost_returnsCreatedPost
```

If the test fails:
- Check the datasource connection / Testcontainers setup
- Verify the Flyway migration applied
- Check DTO ↔ entity mapping logic
- Review Spring Boot startup logs for a stack trace

